    ('German', 'Baseline: reflexively pushes toward the causal chain and imposes origin, cause and rank before the subject matter is considered', 'Causal chain and genealogical ordering', 'Language', 'fusional language / genealogical tendency', 'Tense is obligatory on almost every verb; subject acts, object suffers, clause justifies', 'when the event lies on the time line', 'verb', '["causal", "genealogical", "hierarchy", "tense", "baseline"]', '["Causality", "Agency & control", "Rank & salience", "Time & aspect"]', 'Hawkins, A Comparative Typology of English and German: Unifying the Contrasts (1986)', 'sourced'),
    ('English', 'Pushes toward shorter, parallel units instead of nested causal constructions and reveals things side by side where German stacks them', 'Parallel, short units', 'Language', 'analytic language', 'Prefers parataxis over deep hypotaxis', 'whether the parts are joined side by side or nested', 'connective', '["parallel", "parataxis", "coordination"]', '["Coexistence"]', 'Hawkins, A Comparative Typology of English and German: Unifying the Contrasts (1986)', 'sourced'),
