    ('Anadiplosis', 'Prevents mental jumps: no new argument without the last word of the old one as foundation', 'Gapless chaining without evolutionary jumps', 'Rhetorical figure', 'classical rhetoric / chaining, the end of one step becoming the start of the next', 'The last word or phrase of a clause opens the next, and repeated it builds a chain of linked steps — "Ideas shape actions. Actions shape character." Nothing to do with the ghazal, whose own chaining device is the radif', 'whether each step starts from the end of the last', 'connective', '["anadiplosis", "chaining", "cohesion"]', '["Causality"]', 'Greene et al. (eds.), The Princeton Encyclopedia of Poetry and Poetics (4th ed., 2012)', 'sourced'),
